# Copy to .env.local for `npm run dev`, and set the same values as GitHub repo
# *variables* (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> Variables) so
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml can bake them into the static export.
#
# PASTE THESE AS PLAIN TEXT. Both values travel in an HTTP header, so a single character
# that is not plain ASCII breaks every request with "String contains non ISO-8859-1 code
# point" - a message naming no variable and no file. Copying through anything that
# autocorrects (a doc, a chat client, a notes app) turns a hyphen into an en dash or adds
# a zero-width space, and neither is visible in the settings box afterwards.
# src/lib/supabase-client.ts checks for this at startup and says exactly what is wrong.
#
# Both are meant to ship in the client bundle: the anon key is not a secret, Row Level
# Security on every table (supabase/migrations/0001_accounts.sql) is what actually protects
# player data. Get these from your Supabase project: Project Settings -> API.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Analytics ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The site name registered with Plausible, e.g. "plantdex.example". This is the single
# switch for analytics: leave it blank and no script is loaded and no event is sent, which
# is the right setting for local development, for CI and for any fork. Nothing personally
# identifying is ever attached to an event, because track() takes an event name and has no
# second parameter to attach anything with - see src/lib/analytics.ts. That is also what
# makes Plausible's cheapest plan sufficient: custom properties are a Business-tier feature
# and this schema sends none. Whatever is set here is described on /privacy; the two are
# kept in step by src/lib/legal.test.ts.
#
# Every custom event must also be created as a GOAL in the Plausible dashboard or it records
# nothing visible. The exact list to create is PLAUSIBLE_GOALS in src/lib/analytics.ts.

NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=

# ── Commerce ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Stripe Payment Link for the printed deck, e.g. "https://buy.stripe.com/xxxxxxxx",
# and the price exactly as it should be displayed, e.g. "$24.99".
#
# BOTH are required before /shop shows a buy button. With either missing the page renders an
# honest "not on sale yet" state instead - it never guesses a price, a delivery time or a
# shipping destination, because those are commercial claims nobody has made yet.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DECK_PRICE must match the Payment Link's own price. Stripe is the system of
# record; this string is only what the page prints, and the checkout is authoritative if the
# two ever disagree.
#
# A Payment Link is a shareable URL and carries no secret, which is why it is safe to ship in
# the client bundle. NO STRIPE API KEY BELONGS ANYWHERE IN THIS REPOSITORY - not a secret
# key, and not a publishable one, because Payment Links need neither. src/lib/shop.test.ts
# fails the build if one appears.

NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PAYMENT_LINK=
NEXT_PUBLIC_DECK_PRICE=
